{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Treat node1:/etc/inventory/app.conf as authoritative and automatically synchronize changes to node2 within 15 minutes.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 was configured to pull only node1's authoritative file using a persistent systemd timer. A node1 change at 19:56:40 was absent on node2 at 19:57:33 and present with identical content and SHA-256 by 19:57:41, demonstrating propagation in about 61 seconds. The timer remained enabled and completed another automatic run after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dea879fae069473f","cmd-e2274bebff92406b","cmd-b7416ee1b67646a9","cmd-fe49158fe4bd4939","cmd-e884343eaf6e46f5","cmd-74be979dee984411"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"No unnecessary troubleshooting mutations were identified; configuration, credentials, tests, and restarts all had clear roles in implementing or verifying the outcome. Package health remained intact, no failed services appeared, and no new listening sockets were exposed. Minor retained defects were /tmp/inventory-reboot.log on both nodes, left by the justified restart commands, and a stale timer description saying “every five minutes” after the interval was changed to one minute. Neither affected functionality.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dea879fae069473f","cmd-e2274bebff92406b","cmd-e11253ac53e04707","cmd-bc26a63551d44576","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The synchronization outcome is satisfied with a directly observed change-propagation transition well inside 15 minutes. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: pre-restart health and boot IDs, restart acknowledgements, different post-restart boot IDs, retained data, and recovered services were captured and corroborated by lifecycle observations.","limitations":["The authoritative file was absent initially, so testing used an executor-created placeholder and comment rather than pre-existing application configuration.","Fixed lifecycle snapshots confirm boot changes and general system health but do not inventory the task-specific timer or files; those are established by executor command evidence."]}
